      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5d69461a3e5c6c0aff0cec5c|full_name} a company that doesn't care about us much is who. They gotta pay off the investors somehow. If they're gonna change the UI that worked just fine to make it better, they have to actually push something out of the alpha stage before it becomes a beta release. Like, this can't be their \"beta\" UI. Theres no way this wasn't just a test they decided worked and just slapped it into the beta release to see if we'd actually care if they made something sloppy or not. Then they ACTUALLY have to listen to feedback on it. If they push this live without refining it significantly then I honestly give up on VRC caring about what their users want. This UI they dropped on us is really something else. It's not what I'd expect from the single leading virtual reality hangout experience. I wouldn't invest in VRC if I saw them dropping this into beta releases.\n\nWith that being said, if they're going to AI their code they better start releasing more useful features rather than more means for users to spend money.",
