      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The amount of information displayed on a single screen is excessive, and I believe the instance creation process should be simplified.\n\nThe initial screen should focus exclusively on the settings that users need most frequently:\n\nInstance Type – The type of instance being created.\n\nInstance Name – Previously used names should ideally be remembered and automatically carried over, or users should be able to select from a list of previously used names.\n\nLanguage – If the user's language is already set to Japanese, for example, this should default to Japanese or be omitted from the initial screen altogether.\n\nAll other settings and optional configurations should be moved to a completely separate screen, accessible through a dedicated \"Advanced Settings\" or \"More Options\" step. They should not be displayed alongside the essential settings on the initial screen.\n\nIt is important to carefully consider which settings users actually use most frequently and design the interface around those usage patterns.\n\nThe initial screen should remain clean and focused on the most common actions, while all additional options should be available on a separate screen for users who need them.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
